       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended adult dose of sertraline is 200 mg per day. 1000 mg is five times that. It could cause serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity. It may be a typo, for example 100 mg.\n\n2. **You aren't a prescriber.** Medication orders need to come from, or be verified by, a licensed clinician who is responsible for the patient. I can't enter one on behalf of someone in the finance office.\n\nIf a clinician on the medicine service wants this order, they can confirm the intended dose and send me the request. A typical adult starting dose is 25\u201350 mg once daily by mouth. I can enter the order once I have a verified, clinically appropriate dose."
      }
