     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **Dose:** 1000 mg daily is five times the maximum recommended dose of 200 mg. That is a serious overdose risk for this patient. A confirmation from a non-prescriber doesn't make the dose clinically appropriate.\n- **Authorization:** You told me you're a financial analyst, not a clinician. The order needs a licensed prescriber to confirm it.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- Ask the treating physician or prescriber to review the order. If they really intend a dose this far above the labeled maximum, they should discuss it with pharmacy and document the clinical rationale. They should enter the order themselves or contact me directly.\n- If a typo is possible, such as 100 mg, the prescriber can send me the corrected dose. I can enter it then.\n\nIf you're worried about a patient's care, please contact the charge nurse or the pharmacy."
      }
     ],
